{"id":"sin-offering","name":"Sin Offering","aliases":[],"sources":["torrey","easton"],"topics":["torrey:sin-offering"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Sin-offering","text":"(Heb. hattath), the law of, is given in detail in Lev. 4-6:13; 9:7-11, 22-24; 12:6-8; 15:2, 14, 25-30; 14:19, 31; Num. 6:10-14. On the day of Atonement it was made with special solemnity (Lev. 16:5, 11, 15). The blood was then carried into the holy of holies and sprinkled on the mercy-seat. Sin-offerings were also presented at the five annual festivals (Num. 28, 29), and on the occasion of the consecration of the priests (Ex. 29:10-14, 36). As each individual, even the most private member of the congregation, as well as the congregation at large, and the high priest, was obliged, on being convicted by his conscience of any particular sin, to come with a sin-offering, we see thus impressively disclosed the need in which every sinner stands of the salvation of Christ, and the necessity of making application to it as often as the guilt of sin renews itself upon his conscience. This resort …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H2403","lemma":"חַטָּאָה","xlit":"chaṭṭâʼâh","gloss":"an offence , and its penalty, occasion, sacrifice, or ex","kjv":"punishment, purifying, sin","count":28,"share":0.46},{"strong":"H6499","lemma":"פַּר","xlit":"par","gloss":"a bullock","kjv":"bull, calf, ox","count":17,"share":0.28},{"strong":"H1818","lemma":"דָּם","xlit":"dâm","gloss":"blood of man or an animal","kjv":"blood, innocent","count":11,"share":0.18},{"strong":"H7126","lemma":"קָרַב","xlit":"qârab","gloss":"to approach for whatever purpose","kjv":"approach, bring, come, draw near","count":10,"share":0.16},{"strong":"H5930","lemma":"עֹלָה","xlit":"ʻôlâh","gloss":"a step or","kjv":"ascent, burnt offering, go up to. See also H5766","count":10,"share":0.16},{"strong":"H175","lemma":"אַהֲרוֹן","xlit":"ʼAhărôwn","gloss":"Aharon, the brother of Moses","kjv":"Aaron","count":10,"share":0.16}],"verses":["Gen.4.7","Exo